From 3012d8dc89f454c34c7fb8dcfbf5a9e3866921aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:54:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] MIG-1 F-A (2/2): branch-union, timed-conditional and
 length-counter specs

Fill Turing.FinTM.branchTM_spaceUsed (Simulation), timedCondTM_computes and
timedCondTM_spaceUsed (Wrappers), lengthBitsTM_computes and
lengthBitsTM_spaceUsed (TimeConstructible). The intrinsic space arguments are
relocated from Catalog's private copies (f2_branch_space, f2_cond_ledger /
f2_cond_space, f2_counter_count_space / f2_counter_heads / f2_counter_space)
to the witnesses' homes, using Fin.sum_univ_add (approved import
Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin in Simulation), mem_visitedByTapeHead_iff,
spaceUsed_eq_sum, spaceUsedByTape_eq_card, workTapePos_runFrom_mem_Icc and
exists_first_halt instead of copies. The Catalog sources are deleted in F-D.
Re-point computesFunInTime_cond and timeConstructible_id to the specs.
MIG-24 T1 (Simulation part): one private first-step lemma for
rewind_from_any, timed_rewind and rewind_heads.
